PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1,3},{2,5},{4}}

Chapter 39 is Mumashino in the standard 54-chapter ordering. In the Kō no zu table that is reproduced in the standard editions the incense diagram for Mumashino is drawn with the five vertical bars in the usual left-to-right order, but the numbering convention used in the classical kōdō manuals numbers the bars from the right-hand side of the diagram. Under the left-to-right numbering {1,2,3,4,5} that is normally used for the set-theoretic description this gives a first bar that shares its scent with the third bar, a second bar that shares its scent with the fifth bar, and the fourth bar standing alone.

Hence with the bars labelled 1–5 left to right the equivalence relation is 1 ~ 3, 2 ~ 5 and 4 alone, i.e. the partition {{1,3},{2,5},{4}}. This is the pattern recorded for Mumashino in the incense-chapter concordances and it matches the two-pair-plus-singleton shape that is typical for the late middle part of the work.

